irectories `/opt`, `/home`, and `/srv`. The timestamp of `/out/cvm` implies it was built around the image creation, yet the task suggests `target.c` should exist. I'm also investigating indirect methods, such as using `strace` or `gdb` on the executable to reveal its file access patterns, or searching for embedded paths within the binary.\n\n**Exploring Root Directory**\n\nI am now systematically exploring the root directory, considering that `target.c` might be hidden at the top level or within less common subdirectories. I'm also re-evaluating the problem statement's implication that `target.c` needs implementation, suggesting it might be missing or require manual creation.\n\n",
